1. Introduction
Project 2 develops an API/web service that implements functions from Project 1. The application uses Next.js 14 with the App Router, React, TypeScript, and PostgreSQL. It provides authentication, a protected dashboard, and API routes for students, courses, enrolments, fees, lecturers, and course assignments.
2. Objectives
• Develop a Next.js 14 application with registration, login, and dashboard pages.
• Connect the application to the PostgreSQL database created in Project 1.
• Expose web-service endpoints for the main database functions.
• Allow authenticated users to view and manage student, lecturer, enrolment, and fee information.
• Return the outstanding-fees result from the PostgreSQL function through an API endpoint.
